# Vercel builds only the storefront (the project's Root Directory is
# lorikam-storefront). Everything here is either irrelevant to that build or a
# local artifact, and without this file the CLI uploads ~78MB per deploy.
#
# Note the deploy must be run from the REPO ROOT, not from inside
# lorikam-storefront: the project's Root Directory is already
# "lorikam-storefront", so deploying from within that folder makes Vercel look
# for lorikam-storefront/lorikam-storefront and fail with
# "The specified Root Directory ... does not exist".
#
# EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN HERE IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, ON PURPOSE.
# These are gitignore-style patterns: an unanchored "lorikam/" matches a
# directory with that name at ANY depth. The first version of this file used
# exactly that, and silently deleted
#   lorikam-storefront/src/app/[countryCode]/(main)/lorikam/   (the route)
#   lorikam-storefront/src/modules/lorikam/                    (its components)
# from the upload. The build still succeeded - the route was simply absent from
# the output - and /ro/lorikam returned 404 in production while the homepage
# kept linking to it.

# The Medusa backend deploys to Railway, not here.
/lorikam/

# Railway infrastructure-as-code and its wrapper scripts.
/.railway/
/scripts/
/railway-plan.json

# Local build output and package-manager caches.
.next/
.yarn/cache/
.yarn/install-state.gz
node_modules/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Local env files - Vercel holds the real values as project env vars.
.env.local
/.env.railway

# Test and tooling leftovers.
/.playwright-mcp/
